-- title:
--   Crossing presentation ̂ A[[U,V]]/(UV-varpi^m) at the ends, with diagonal action
-- statement:
--   Fix primes $q\ge 5$ and $\ell\ge 3$ with $\ell\neq q$, and a non-zero natural number $M'$ with $q\nmid M'$ and $\ell\nmid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero, $\xi\in L$ a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity, and assume (`hι`) that there is a ring homomorphism $\iota:L\to\mathbb C$ with $\iota\xi=e^{2\pi i/(q\ell)}$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L\subseteq L(\!(T)\!)$ which (`hK`) is the $L$-subfield of $L(\!(T)\!)$ generated by the coefficientwise images of the $q$-expansion function field over $\mathbb Q$ of $X_H$ of level $(q\ell)^2M'$, where $H=\ker\bigl((\mathbb Z/(q\ell)^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q\ell)^\times\bigr)$ is the group of units congruent to $1$ modulo $q\ell$. Let $A$ be a henselian discrete valuation ring with algebraically closed residue field, equipped with an $L$-algebra structure making $L$ its fraction field, with $q\in\mathfrak m_A$ and $\xi$ in the image of $A$, and let $K$ be an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$. Let $j\in K$ be non-zero with Laurent series the image [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of the classical $j$-series, let $\varpi$ generate $\mathfrak m_A$, and let $\varpi_t\in A$ satisfy $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1}=q\cdot(\text{unit})$. Write $C=$ `chartAlgFin A K j` for the integral closure of $A[j]$ in $K$, and let $y\subset C$ be a maximal ideal containing $\varpi$ which is supersingular in the sense (`hss`) that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi:C\to\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the element $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of $j_0\in\Omega$ such that every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $j_0$ has no non-zero $q$-torsion point. Throughout, $\mathfrak X=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) denotes the two-chart integral model (the pushout of the two affine charts $\operatorname{Spec}C$ and $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the integral closure of $A[j^{-1}]$), `toBase` its structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec}A$, and `ιFin` the morphism from $\operatorname{Spec}C$; and for $\gamma\in SL_2(\mathbb Z)$ a *level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$* means an $L$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ satisfying [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L (q*ℓ) ξ (q*ℓ) ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q*ℓ) M') γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29), i.e. for all weights $k$, all modular forms $f,g$ for $\Gamma_H((q\ell)^2M')$ with integral $q$-expansions $p_f,p_g$ ($p_g\neq0$ in $L(\!(T)\!)$), all $x\in K$ with Laurent series $p_f/p_g$ and every embedding $L\to\mathbb C$ carrying $\xi$ to $e^{2\pi i/(q\ell)}$, the image of $\tau x$ times the $q$-expansion of $g\mid_k$`conjElemN (q*ℓ) γ⁻¹` equals the $q$-expansion of $f\mid_k$`conjElemN (q*ℓ) γ⁻¹`.
--
--   The hypothesis `hArig` is the global Drinfeld-chart block: for every point $z$ of $\mathfrak X$ at which the image of $\varpi$ lies in $\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O_{\mathfrak X,z}}$, every point $y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec}C$ with `ιFin` $y'=z$ whose ideal is supersingular in the above sense, there exist a complete discrete valuation ring $W$ which is a domain, a ring homomorphism $\sigma:A\to W$ with $\mathfrak m_W=(\sigma\varpi)$, power series $f,u,v\in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u,v$ units and $f\equiv$ [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.drinfeldForm q W`](def/DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart.html#L18) $=X_0X_1^q-X_0^qX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the $\mathfrak m$-adic completion of the stalk $\mathcal O_{\mathfrak X,z}$ onto $S=W[[X_0,X_1]]/\bigl(C(\sigma(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))v-fu\bigr)$, subject to seven groups of riders (summarised here): *constants*, $e$ carries the image of $a\in A$ to the class of $C(\sigma a)$; *chart stability*, every level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ maps $C$ into $C$; *fixing*, for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')\cap\Gamma(\ell)$ the induced map satisfies $\tau a-a\in y'$ for all $a\in C$; *tangent action*, for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ fixing $y'$ in this sense there are an automorphism $\theta$ of $S$ compatible with $\tau$ through $e$ and the germ map, fixing constants, with $\theta(X_j)\equiv\sum_i M_{ij}X_i$ modulo the square of the ideal generated by the classes of $X_0,X_1$, together with $c\in W$ and $M\in M_2(W)$ such that $c^{q+1}\equiv1$, $M_{ij}\equiv c\,\gamma_{ij}$ modulo $\mathfrak m_W$, $c\equiv1$ when $\gamma\in\Gamma(\ell)$, and $c\not\equiv1$ when $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau\neq\mathrm{id}$; *branch separation*, two primes of $S$ over $\sigma\varpi$, neither containing both coordinate classes and each containing a form $a_iX_0+b_iX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^2$ with $q\nmid a_1b_2-a_2b_1$, have distinct contractions to the stalk; *integrality*, for a prime $P$ of $S$ over $\sigma\varpi$ not containing both coordinate classes and containing $X_0$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^2$, an element $a\in C$ has germ in the contraction of $P$ exactly when all Laurent coefficients of $a$ lie in the image of $\mathfrak m_A$; and *Hasse*, the Laurent series [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L (q*ℓ)`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) lies in $K$ and in $C$, is congruent modulo $y'$ to some $a_0\in A$, and the difference has image under $e$ the class of a series $h\in(X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ with $e_0\ge1$ whose degree-$e_0$ form $\sum_{i\le e_0}\operatorname{coeff}_{(i,e_0-i)}(h)a^ib^{e_0-i}$ is a unit for all $a,b\in W$ not both in $\mathfrak m_W$ with $a^qb-ab^q\in\mathfrak m_W$.
--
--   Next, a particular point is pinned: $z$ with the image $\varpi_z$ of $\varpi$ in $\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O_{\mathfrak X,z}}$, a point $y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec}C$ with `ιFin` $y'=z$, supersingular (`hss'`) and with $y'$ equal to $y$ (`hy'y`); and one chart witness $W_1,\sigma_1,f_1,u_1,v_1$ (with $u_1,v_1$ units and $f_1$ congruent to the Drinfeld form modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$) together with $e_1:\widehat{\mathcal O}_{\mathfrak X,z}\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }S=W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/\bigl(C(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))v_1-f_1u_1\bigr)$, and the hypothesis `hW₁`, which asserts the same seven groups of riders (constants, chart stability, fixing, tangent action, branch separation, integrality, Hasse) for this witness.
--
--   The weighted centre is pinned by `hJ`: $J$ is the infimum, over all $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and all level automorphisms $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $C$, of the preimage under $\tau|_C$ of the contraction along $e_1\circ(\text{germ at }z)$ of the ideal of $S$ generated by the classes of $C(\sigma_1\varpi_t)$, $X_0$ and $X_1$. The ring $B$ is pinned by `hB`: $B=C[J/\varpi_t]$, the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ obtained from $C$ by adjoining all $x\in K$ with $x\varpi_t\in J$. Finally $W$ is a valuation subring of $K$ containing $B$ (`hBW`), subject to four blocks: `hR1`, $C\subseteq B$ and every element of $K$ is a quotient of elements of $B$ with non-zero denominator; `hR2`, $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A$ and $B/\varpi B$ has Krull dimension $\le1$; `hR3` (five clauses), $W\cap L$ is the image of $A$, $\mathfrak m_W$ is generated by $\varpi$, $W$ is a discrete valuation ring, $y=\mathfrak m_W\cap C$, and $W$ is the localisation of $B$ at $\mathfrak m_W\cap B$; and `hEQ` (five clauses), namely: for every $\mathbb F_{q^2}$-algebra structure on the residue field $k$ of $A$ there is a surjection $\rho:B\to$ [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q k`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) $=k[x_0,x_1]/(\mathrm{drinfeldPoly}_q-1)$ with kernel $\mathfrak m_W\cap B$, compatible with $A\to k$, and such that every level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ preserving $W$ is intertwined by $\rho$ with [`DrinfeldCurve.hAction`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L325) of a pair $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,c)$ in [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) (the kernel of the character $(\bar g,c)\mapsto\det(\bar g)\,c^{q+1}$), with $c\neq1$ when $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau\neq\mathrm{id}$; $B$ is stable under all such $\tau$; every prime $Q$ of $B$ containing $\varpi$ contains $\tau(\mathfrak m_W\cap B)$ for some admissible pair $(\gamma,\tau)$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$; an element of $B$ carried into $\mathfrak m_W$ by all such $\tau$ is divisible by $\varpi$ in $B$; and a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ preserves $W$ as soon as it preserves $y$ on $C$ in both directions.
--
--   The cyclicity data are: $n\ge1$ with $n\mid q+1$; $\gamma_0\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and a level automorphism $\tau_0$ at $\gamma_0^{-1}$ preserving $W$; `hcyc1`, $\tau_0^n$ fixes $B$ pointwise; `hcyc2`, $\tau_0^k$ does not fix $B$ pointwise for $0<k<n$; `hcyc3`, every level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ preserving $W$ agrees on $B$ with $\tau_0^k$ for some $k<n$.
--
--   Conclusion. There exist $m\ge1$ with $\varpi^m=\varpi_t\cdot(\text{unit of }A)$, and an element $\zeta_0$ of $\hat A=$ `AdicCompletion (maximalIdeal A) A` with $\zeta_0^n=1$ and $\zeta_0^k-1$ a unit for $0<k<n$, such that the following holds for every subring $O\subseteq K$ subject to the two conditions: (a) there are $a\in J\subseteq C$ with $a\neq0$ in $K$ and a maximal ideal $P$ of the blow-up chart $B_a=C[J/a]$ (the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ generated over $C$ by all $x\in K$ with $xa\in J$) such that $O$ is the localisation of $B_a$ at $P$, every element of $y$ lying in $O$ is a non-unit of $O$, and $B\not\subseteq O$; and (b) $O$ is $\tau_0$-stable, $f\in O\iff\tau_0f\in O$. Then $O\subseteq W$; moreover $O$ is local and Noetherian and:
--
--   $C\subseteq O$; $O\cap L$ is the image of $A$; every $f\in O$ differs from the image of some element of $A$ by a non-unit of $O$; and, writing $\Lambda=$ `UVCrossingModel` $\hat A$ $(\varpi^m)=\hat A[[X_0,X_1]]/(X_0X_1-C(\varpi^m))$ (with $\varpi$ taken in $\hat A$), there exist $c_x,c_y\in O$, a unit $u$ of $O$, a ring isomorphism $\iota$ from the $\mathfrak m_O$-adic completion of $O$ onto $\Lambda$, units $\gamma_U,\gamma_V$ of $\Lambda$, an $\hat A$-algebra automorphism $\theta_0$ of $\Lambda$, an element $\zeta_0'$ with $\zeta_0\zeta_0'=1$, and a local ring structure on $\Lambda$, such that: $c_xc_y=\varpi^m u$ in $O$; $\iota$ carries the image of $a\in A$ to `UVCrossingModel.const` of $a$; $\iota(c_x)=\gamma_U\cdot$`UVCrossingModel.U` and $\iota(c_y)=\gamma_V\cdot$`UVCrossingModel.V`; if $c_y$ lies in $W$ then it lies in $\mathfrak m_W$, while if $c_x$ lies in $W$ then it does not; $\iota$ intertwines $\tau_0$ on $O$ with $\theta_0$ on $\Lambda$; and finally $\theta_0(U)-\mathrm{const}(\zeta_0)\,U$ and $\theta_0(V)-\mathrm{const}(\zeta_0')\,V$ both lie in the square of the maximal ideal of $\Lambda$.
--
--   This is the local analysis of the ends of the blow-up of a supersingular chart of the integral model: each such end has completed local ring the crossing model $\hat A[[U,V]]/(UV-\varpi^m)$ over the completion of the base discrete valuation ring, with the distinguished cyclic automorphism $\tau_0$ acting on the two branches by $\zeta_0$ and $\zeta_0^{-1}$ to first order. It is the producer step used by the cyclic-decomposition assembly for the blown-up supersingular chart, and rests on the Drinfeld-chart presentation of the completed stalks at supersingular points together with the Drinfeld-curve description of the exceptional fibre.
